---
/**
 * ============================================================================
 * OWNER: PLEASE HAVE THIS PRIVACY POLICY REVIEWED BEFORE LAUNCH.
 * This is a plain English template for a small Irish sole trader. It is not legal advice.
 * Ask a solicitor or a data protection adviser to check it against how you actually work.
 * Placeholders (in [SQUARE BRACKETS]) come from the legal section of src/config/site.ts.
 * ============================================================================
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CTASection from '../components/CTASection.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Text from '../components/Text.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import { official } from '../data/official';
import { mailHref } from '../lib/format';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Settle in Ireland"
  description="How Settle in Ireland collects, uses and protects your personal data, how long it is kept, and your rights under GDPR."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Privacy Policy"
    crumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy Policy', href: '/privacy-policy/' }]}
  >
    <p class="mt-4 text-muted">Last updated: <Text value={site.legal.lastUpdated} /></p>
  </PageHero>

  <div class="container-site py-14 lg:py-20">
    <article class="prose-site mx-auto max-w-[46rem] text-[1.02rem]">
      <p class="lead !mt-0">
        This policy explains what personal data Settle in Ireland collects, why, how long it is kept and what your rights are. I have written it in
        plain English. If anything is unclear, please <a href={mailHref('Privacy question')}>email me</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Who I am</h2>
      <p>
        Settle in Ireland is an independent arrival and settling-in support service run by <Text value={site.legal.ownerLegalName} />, a sole trader
        based in Ireland. For the purposes of data protection law, I am the "controller" of the personal data described in this policy.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Email: <a href={mailHref()}>{site.email}</a></li>
        <li>Postal address: <Text value={site.legal.postalAddress} /></li>
        <li>Business registration: <Text value={site.legal.businessRegistration} /></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. What data I collect</h2>
      <p>I only collect the information you, or a partner agency with your consent, choose to send me. This can include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your name, country, email address and phone or WhatsApp number;</li>
        <li>your arrival details, such as your expected arrival date, airport and flight details;</li>
        <li>your college or course, and the name of the partner agency that referred you;</li>
        <li>your accommodation address in Ireland, once you have one;</li>
        <li>the services you are interested in and the messages you send me;</li>
        <li>payment records, such as the amount and date of each payment.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        While I help you prepare for official processes, you may choose to show me or send me copies of documents, such as letters or forms. I only
        ask for what is needed to help you, and I do not keep copies longer than necessary. Please never send me passwords, PINs, security codes or
        full bank card details.
      </p>
      <p>
        I do not ask for sensitive information, such as health information. If you choose to share something like this, for example when asking for
        help finding a GP, I only use it for that purpose.
      </p>

      <h2>3. The website and the enquiry forms</h2>
      <p>
        The enquiry forms on this website do not send or store anything. When you press the button, your answers are turned into a message that opens
        in WhatsApp or in your email app. Nothing reaches me until you choose to press send there.
      </p>
      <p>
        This website does not use cookies, tracking or advertising tools, and it does not store your form answers in your browser. Fonts are hosted on
        this website itself, so no information is sent to font providers. Like all websites, the hosting provider may keep basic technical logs, such
        as IP addresses, for security and to keep the website running.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Why I use your data, and the legal basis</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>To reply to your enquiry</strong>, because you asked me to and it is a step before a possible agreement.</li>
        <li><strong>To provide the service</strong> you or your partner agency arranged, which is necessary for our agreement.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>To update your partner agency or family</strong> about your arrival and progress, but only with your consent. You can withdraw your
          consent at any time.
        </li>
        <li><strong>To keep financial records</strong>, because Irish tax law requires it.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Partner agencies</h2>
      <p>
        If a partner agency refers you, they share your details with me only after you have agreed. I share updates about your arrival and progress
        with the agency only at the milestones you have agreed to. I never sell your data or share it for marketing.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Who else processes your data</h2>
      <p>I use a small number of everyday services to communicate and run the business:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>WhatsApp</strong> (Meta), for messages and calls;</li>
        <li><strong>my email provider</strong>, for emails;</li>
        <li><strong>my website host</strong>, which serves this website;</li>
        <li><strong>an accountant</strong>, if needed, for financial records.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        WhatsApp and email providers process messages under their own privacy policies and terms. Some of these providers may process data outside
        the European Economic Area, using the safeguards required by law. I only share your data with public authorities if the law requires it.
      </p>

      <h2>7. How long I keep your data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Enquiries that do not go ahead: deleted within <Text value="[12 months]" /> of our last contact.</li>
        <li>Client records: kept for the length of the service and up to <Text value="[12 months]" /> after it ends, then deleted.</li>
        <li>Copies of documents: deleted as soon as they are no longer needed to help you.</li>
        <li>Payment and financial records: kept for six years, as Irish tax law requires.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>ask for a copy of the personal data I hold about you;</li>
        <li>ask me to correct data that is wrong or incomplete;</li>
        <li>ask me to delete your data;</li>
        <li>ask me to limit how I use your data, or object to how I use it;</li>
        <li>ask for your data in a format you can take elsewhere;</li>
        <li>withdraw your consent at any time, where I rely on consent.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To use any of these rights, <a href={mailHref('Data protection request')}>email me</a>. I will reply within one month, as the law requires.
        You can also ask me to delete our WhatsApp conversation, but please note that WhatsApp and your own phone keep their own copies.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Complaints</h2>
      <p>
        If you are unhappy with how I handle your data, please contact me first so I can try to put it right. You also have the right to complain to the
        Data Protection Commission, the Irish data protection authority, at
        <a href={official.dpc.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.dataprotection.ie</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Keeping your data safe</h2>
      <p>
        I take reasonable steps to protect your data, such as using secure devices and accounts protected with strong passwords. I only keep what I
        need.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Clients under 18</h2>
      <p>If you are under 18, please ask a parent or guardian to contact me on your behalf.</p>

      <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>If I change this policy, I will update it on this page and change the date at the top.</p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <CTASection title="Questions about your data?" text={`Send me a message or an email and I will help. ${site.responseTime}`} />
</BaseLayout>
